# Example 17: The repressilator - synthetic oscillatory network (Elowitz & Leibler 2000)
# Three repressor genes in a cyclic negative-feedback loop:
#
#     LacI represses tetR transcription (PLlacO1 hybrid promoter)
#     TetR represses cI   transcription (PLtetO1 hybrid promoter)
#     cI   represses lacI transcription (l PR promoter)
#
# Measured parameters (Elowitz & Leibler, Nature 403:335-338, 2000, DOI:10.1038/35002125):
#   - oscillation period ~150 min (peak-to-peak 160 +/- 40 min, n = 63 cells),
#     about three times the 50-70 min cell-division time, so the clock state is
#     transmitted from generation to generation
#   - repressor stability reduced ~10x by C-terminal ssrA degradation tags
#     (~60 min half-life untagged -> ~4 min tagged), favouring the oscillatory regime
#   - the continuous model (Box 1) shows limit cycles for strong, tightly-repressible
#     promoters with cooperative repression and comparable mRNA/protein decay;
#     weaker repression relaxes to a stable steady state instead
#
# HelixLang maps the network onto a discrete GRN with 1 tick = 1 minute. The
# #regulate cycle below declares the same negative-feedback topology. Because the
# discrete, synchronous GRN has no time delays and no basal (leaky) synthesis, it
# relaxes to the symmetric fixed point rather than oscillating; the sustained limit
# cycle emerges in the continuous-time model (Elowitz & Leibler 2000, Box 1), so the
# Python API below sets up the equivalent Hill-kinetics network for scripting.

#promoter name=p_lac_repressed strength=0.9   # PLlacO1: strong, LacI-repressible
#promoter name=p_tet_repressed strength=0.9   # PLtetO1: strong, TetR-repressible
#promoter name=p_ci_repressed  strength=0.9   # PR: strong, cI-repressible

#gene name=lacI promoter=p_ci_repressed
ATG GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

#gene name=tetR promoter=p_lac_repressed
ATG GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

#gene name=cI promoter=p_tet_repressed
ATG GCT GCT GCT TAA
#end

#regulate lacI -> p_lac_repressed strength=-0.9
#regulate tetR -> p_tet_repressed strength=-0.9
#regulate cI -> p_ci_repressed strength=-0.9

